Description: xdg-activation: let user actions hand focus on reliably
 Mir's xdg-activation carried GNOME-style focus stealing prevention, and it
 left the window a click asked for in the background:
  - only the focused client got a real token, so the top bar (a layer
    surface, never keyboard-focused) got a bogus one when a notification
    was clicked, and Telegram could not come forward;
  - any key press, or focus moving to another client, revoked every
    pending token, so typing while an app started up kept it behind;
  - tokens expired after 3 seconds.
 A client now also gets a real token when it names the serial of an input
 event it received (the user is interacting with it), key presses and
 focus changes no longer revoke tokens, and they last 30 seconds. Tokens
 are still single use. The token authority unit test waits for the new
 timeout.
Author: Umoja developers
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-11
